  "limitations": [
    "the clearance is a hypothetical rigid translation used to measure how large a gap the overlap needs; no scene is modified and no anatomy is changed",
    "displacing tibia-side muscle meshes with the tibia assumes they follow that segment, which is how the research layer already drives them",
    "penetration depth and the deepest point come from intersecting face centroids, so they are estimates rather than measured overlap volumes",
    "the deepest point is characterised by its distance to the model's knee joint centre and by projections on the two segment axes; that centre is a model joint, not a fitted anatomical landmark",
    "no published cartilage or meniscus thickness was checked in this round, so the measured clearance is reported as geometry only, not as a physiological requirement",
    "one standing registration, one subject's squat, right side only"
  ]
